From 9b51ff8d5bdec0db0ba377239a5bc3f9c6adb22f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:27:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 188/215] fix: sharp, unhazed ray traced reflections and a
 provable sun shadow at the hit

Stage 2C, shader side. Five findings, all inside %_RT_QUALITY / %_RT_PARTICLE_SHADOW
blocks or behind a per-pixel predicate that is a compile-time false off the flag.

(a) A normal mapped mirror printed its detail map into the reflection as a regular
    grid: the reflect direction was built from the per-pixel shading normal. Neo's
    ti_RT_NormalsFading is transplanted as e_svoTI_RT_NormalsFading and applied to
    the reflecting surface as well as to the hit; the flat normal comes from the
    screen space derivatives of the reconstructed world position.

(b) Blur. Three causes, all cone tracing reconstruction applied to a picture that is
    already final and already full resolution: the stochastic gloss kernel
    (kern += vFocus * power / 25, offset indexed by the screen dither tile, so it is
    also a second source of (a)), portal ray bending (portal chosen by the same tile
    index), the demosaic min/max spread, and UpScalePS's five tap +-1.5 texel kernel
    with its quarter texel centre bias. Triangle rays now take the exact mirror
    direction, and DemosaicPS / UpScalePS collapse to a single tap for RT pixels,
    which is Neo's own answer (neo:1468-1472, neo:2340-2346).

(c) Sun shadow: the cascade walk was structurally correct but unprovable. Debug view
    7 renders the factor directly (white = the hit sees the sun), and the sun lobe is
    now accumulated instead of assigned, which is what Callback_ShadingDirect's out
    parameters actually promise. View 8 renders sun + local lights before probes.

(d) Haze. A ray that hit nothing was still fogged over the full e_svoTI_RT_MaxDistRay
    sentinel, dragging every escaped pixel towards the fog colour; and UpScalePS added
    e_svoTI_DiffuseBias * sky top on top of a fully shaded hit. Both dropped for RT
    pixels. The demosaic and upscale clamps go from 8 to Neo's 100, because that
    channel now carries a real radiance instead of a unit length chroma. Debug view 9
    renders the raw accumulator before fog, clamp and exposure.

(e) Every hit came back with a flat normal and no gloss response:
    RT_ProcessBestHit scaled the normal map by CV_TerrainInfo.y, which Neo uses as its
    normals fading distance but which CE 5.7.1 fills as a hard zero
    (GraphicsPipeline.cpp:1280). Driven off the new cvar lane instead. Debug views 10,
    11 and 12 render the raw atlas normal, the hit smoothness and the hit reflectance
    so the remaining half of the finding can be pinned on the atlas producer.

Validated with scene-notes/rt/tools/rtharness2: ShadePS, ConeTracePS, DemosaicPS and
UpScalePS compile clean in (QUALITY, SAMPLE6), (QUALITY, SAMPLE6, PARTICLE_SHADOW),
(QUALITY) and (SAMPLE4), plus BuildRayTracingLightListCS as cs_5_0.

